### Prisma Nominations API — ejemplos (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
# Datos ficticios. card_id es siempre un token, nunca un PAN.
# Correr en orden: E1 guarda el id y la URI de la nominación para los GET.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@entity = ENT01
@otherEntity = ENT02

### E1 — alta válida: 202 + Location + Idempotent-Replayed: false
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-e1-0001

{
  "request_id": "0b4a9f2e-6c1d-4e7a-8b3f-5d2c1a0e9f87",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_4f9a2c7b8d1e",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("nominationId", response.body.nomination_id);
    client.global.set("location", response.headers.valueOf("Location"));
%}

### Consultar estado (GET por Location)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{location}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### Consultar historial
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{nominationId}}/history
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

### E3 — replay: mismo POST → 202, mismo nomination_id, Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-e3-0001

{
  "request_id": "0b4a9f2e-6c1d-4e7a-8b3f-5d2c1a0e9f87",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_4f9a2c7b8d1e",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

### E3 — conflicto: mismo request_id con otro contenido → 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

{
  "request_id": "0b4a9f2e-6c1d-4e7a-8b3f-5d2c1a0e9f87",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_otra_tarjeta",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

### E3 — mismo request_id en otra entidad → nominación nueva (la clave es por entidad)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{otherEntity}}

{
  "request_id": "0b4a9f2e-6c1d-4e7a-8b3f-5d2c1a0e9f87",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_4f9a2c7b8d1e",
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

### Aislamiento — otra entidad consulta la nominación → 404 NOMINATION_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations/{{nominationId}}
X-Entity-Id: {{otherEntity}}

### E2 — faltan campos obligatorios → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (errors en snake_case)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

{
  "alias": "CUENTA SUELDO"
}

### E2 — card_id con forma de PAN → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (el valor no se devuelve)
# 4111111111111111 es el número de prueba público de Visa, no una tarjeta real.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

{
  "request_id": "5e8c1f3a-2b7d-4c9e-a1f0-3d6b8e2c4a71",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "4111111111111111"
}

### E2 — JSON inválido → 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Entity-Id: {{entity}}

{ "request_id": "no-es-un-uuid", "customer_id": "CUST-000123",

### E2 — falta X-Entity-Id → 400 MISSING_HEADER
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/nominations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "request_id": "9a3d7e1b-4f2c-4b8a-9e6d-1c5f7a2b8d30",
  "customer_id": "CUST-000123",
  "account_id": "0001234567890987654",
  "card_id": "tok_4f9a2c7b8d1e"
}
